  "question": {
    "text": "The equation of the straight line passing through the point $(4,3)$ and making intercepts on the co-ordinate axes whose sum is $-1$ is",
    "image": null
  },
  "options": [
    {
      "id": "q3b7A",
      "text": "\n$\\frac{x}{2}+\\frac{y}{3}=-1$ and $\\frac{x}{-2}+\\frac{y}{1}=-1$\n",
      "image": null,
      "isCorrect": false
    },
    {
      "id": "r2YRE",
      "text": "\n$\\frac{x}{2}-\\frac{y}{3}=-1$ and $\\frac{x}{-2}+\\frac{y}{1}=-1$\n",
      "image": null,
      "isCorrect": false
    },
    {
      "id": "TDUCT",
      "text": "\n$\\frac{x}{2}+\\frac{y}{3}=1$ and $\\frac{x}{2}+\\frac{y}{1}=1$\n",
      "image": null,
      "isCorrect": false
    },
    {
      "id": "Sxiii",
      "text": "\n$\\frac{x}{2}-\\frac{y}{3}=1$ and $\\frac{x}{-2}+\\frac{y}{1}=1$",
      "image": null,
      "isCorrect": true
    }
  ],
  "correctValue": null,
  "solution": {
    "text": "$\\frac{x}{a}+\\frac{y}{b}=1$ where $a+b=-1$ and $\\frac{4}{a}+\\frac{3}{b}=1$\n$\\Rightarrow a=2, b=-3$ or $a=-2, b=1$\nHence $\\frac{x}{2}-\\frac{y}{3}=1$ and $\\frac{x}{-2}+\\frac{y}{1}=1$",
    "image": null
  },
